**/vendor/
# Per-lib locks only. The root keeps its lock: the monorepo root is an
# application-shaped package pinning the whole tree. Each <lib>/ is published
# standalone as sugarcraft/<lib>, and a committed lock there both pins sibling
# revisions a consumer never wanted and makes `composer install` silently
# ignore the CI path-repo injection (install resolves from the lock, warns, and
# exits 0). See docs/plans/leftover/phase-01-pty-quickwins/step-02-drop-consumer-locks.md
/*/composer.lock
.phpunit.result.cache
**/.phpunit.result.cache
.phpunit.cache/
**/.phpunit.cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.log
.cache/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/shell-snapshots
.claude/paste-cache
.claude/file-history
.claude/remote
.claude/worktrees
.claude/history.jsonl
.claude/backups
.claude/mcp-needs-auth-cache.json
.claude/projects
.claude/cache
.claude.json
.claude/.credentials.json
.claude/ide/
.claude/policy-limits.json
.claude/sessions/
.php-cs-fixer.cache

.candy-code-build/
# The release-phar workflow builds into a repo-root dist/ (its explicit
# --out=dist/candy-code.phar; the script's own default lands under candy-code/,
# which that lib's .gitignore already covers). The ROOT-anchored form is
# deliberate: an unanchored dist/ would also swallow candy-code-web/dist/,
# which is committed on purpose. Untracked here, this dirt would falsify
# build-phar's fail-closed dirty-tree preflight (git status --porcelain from
# the candy-code subdir reports the root path as `?? dist/`) — a second local
# build refused by the first (rev-w2j3 N-M3, owner queue 2026-10-19).
/dist/
/.candy-code-prompt/
codacy-coverage-reporter
# E737 housekeeping: the operator's repo-root MCP config is untracked local state that must never
# enter a commit; discovery reads exactly one `$root/.mcp.json`, so the ignore is ROOT-ANCHORED —
# sub-directory project `.mcp.json` files stay committable per-project config (the hazard is the
# operator file sitting at the monorepo root, not the filename).
/.mcp.json
__pycache__/
